          "answer": "**Please get checked urgently today, even though it has gone away.** Call your local emergency number now, or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not wait to see if it happens again.\n\nThe stroke guidance (*Sudden neurological symptoms that may indicate a stroke*) says that sudden face drooping or an uneven smile, and sudden trouble with speech, are treated as a possible stroke until proven otherwise. It says to note the time symptoms started and call emergency services right away. Your symptoms match that pattern: one side of your face changed and your speech was wrong for about ten minutes. That they have settled does not rule out a serious cause, and the guidance does not treat recovery as reassurance.\n\nOur automatic risk check labelled this \"routine\" because it did not match its fixed list. That label should not reassure you. The stroke guidance is the more relevant source here.\n\nIf it happens again, or you notice arm weakness, numbness, vision changes, or a severe sudden headache, call emergency services immediately. Write down what you noticed and the time it started, so you can tell the clinician.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
